PATCH 272: the object-type-A weapon-cooldown emitter FUN_0000_a9a0 -- DGROUP near-offset base-loss
(SIGSEGV), dispatched by the 7c1d object-type-A UPDATE template (patch 244).

ASM-verified (asm 0xa9a0-0xa9e9; DS=DGROUP=0x1c00): di=object near offset arrives in param_1 (7c1d
dispatches its per-object methods with the near offset as arg0), but a9a0's asm reads DI and Ghidra
mapped the object to the uninitialised param_2 -> host-pointer deref SIGSEGV.  a9a0 advances two
cooldown counters ([di+0xa6] gated on [di+0x19]&6, [di+0x52] gated on &0x10), clearing the corresponding
[di+0x19] bits at rollover (0x40 / 0x70) and posting the weapon-cooldown event via bf3c(0x1b)/bf3c(0x23),
all guarded by [di+0x3d]&0xe0 == 0.  Rebased every [di+off] to the DGROUP model; bf3c keeps the object
as a near offset (param_3), matching patch 263.  Mission-cascade only.
